- **Q3 (WP0.9: the candidates' licence terms; STOP-CLASS: S4 must answer it in words).** MEASURED: no candidate is named in the project's documents but the retired Gotenberg / LibreOffice service (`A2:218`, `03:344`), and no licence text of any candidate is in the project folder or the package cache. Default: NO web read; D5 states the constraints (cited), the licence checklist, the one named candidate with its terms UNMEASURED, and that the candidate list is owed (a QUESTION, whose: Tuesday then the product owner). Alternative A: Tuesday names the candidates and, for each, ONE public licence page (no sign-in, no HP, Microsoft or Datasec host) in S4; the seat reads each by one GET and quotes the terms with URL and time. Alternative B: drop D5 from this lane. Cost of the default: D5 is a short checklist, the licence read still owed before S12; cost of A: the seat reaches public hosts (the first HTTP of this lane beyond Jira), and a licence page is not the licence file a release would ship; cost of B: WP0.9's free half stays undone.
